      "message": "I would suggest not to change the name for now (until we come out with a better idea).\n\nReason:\n- There are interrupt_disable() and interrupt_enable().  disable_int() is confusing (in the whole context).\n- get_int_mask() and set_int_mask() are pair-existing.  If get_int_mask() changes to disable_int(); then set_int_mask() should change to something similar to \"enable_int()\".  However, it is not.  set_int_mask() is restoring the mie (and not necessarily enable interrupt).\n- The get_ and set_ concept here is more closed to get_ and put_ in kernel.\n\nI would suggest leave it as is.  We can refactor them when we get a better shape of it.",
